          "content": "Start each study by sketching the optical interface or mode profile and locating energy channels: reflection, transmission, absorption, scattering, any luminescence and electrical conversion. Use a vacuum wavelength unless clearly stated otherwise. Predict limiting behavior of the equation and identify its domain before entering numbers. For numerical exercises, report input units, intermediate quantities, numerical precision and a reasonableness check. The two model cards in each unit are simple independent controls, not coupled predictions of a fabricated device. The capstone demands a falsifiable physical explanation and a feasible characterization plan.",
